IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `er6-part-vii-transitional`
IMPORT `er6-schedule-iii-interim-provisions`

-- Tests of Schedule III (SOR-96-332.txt lines 2244-2369). Expected values are written from the text, not from the rules.
-- The maximum weekly insurable earnings are the Act's, not this piece's: the Act's Schedule II item 1 (interim section 4(2), source line 3252 of
-- the Act, piece ei6) gives $750 (the subsection names no year), so "20 per cent" is 150 and the multiples used below are 2 1/6 x 150 = 325, 4 1/3 x 150 = 650.
-- Days: Part I applies 1996-06-30 to 1996-12-31; Part I.1 1996-09-12 to 1996-12-31; Part II item 2 (ss 19 to 21) 1996-06-30 to 1996-12-31;
-- items 3 to 6 1996-06-30 to 1997-01-04 (reg 95(4), (4.1), (5) with (2) and (3)).

`test pay period facts` cash hours eachCash eachWork MEANS `er6 Earnings and hours in a pay period` WITH
    `cash earnings for the pay period` IS cash
    `total number of hours of employment in the pay period` IS hours
    `cash earnings for each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS eachCash
    `employment in each week, part of a week or period of seven days in the pay period` IS eachWork

§ `Part I -- s 6.1(1): the amount, the exclusion`

#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the amount of cash earnings` 750 EQUALS 150
-- argument order: a day in the week; cash earnings in the week; hours employed in the week; maximum weekly insurable earnings; subsection (2) says (1) does not apply
-- 20 per cent of 750 is 150: 149 is under it, 150 is not
-- "cash earnings are less than 20 per cent ... and who is employed for less than 15 hours": both limbs
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` (YMD 1996 7 14) 149 14 750 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` (YMD 1996 7 14) 150 14 750 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` (YMD 1996 7 14) 149 15 750 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` (YMD 1996 7 14) 500 20 750 FALSE)
-- "Subject to subsection (2)"
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` (YMD 1996 7 14) 149 14 750 TRUE)
-- the period in which Part I applies
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` (YMD 1996 6 29) 149 14 750 FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` (YMD 1996 6 30) 149 14 750 FALSE
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` (YMD 1996 12 31) 149 14 750 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(1) the employment in the week is excluded from insurable employment` (YMD 1997 1 1) 149 14 750 FALSE)

§ `Part I -- s 6.1(2): the exceptions for pay periods`

-- (a) a multiple of a week (two weeks here): earnings of a like multiple of the amount (300), or hours of a like multiple of 15 (30)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 a multiple of a week` 2) (`test pay period facts` 300 0 TRUE FALSE) 750
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 a multiple of a week` 2) (`test pay period facts` 299 0 TRUE FALSE) 750)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 a multiple of a week` 2) (`test pay period facts` 0 30 FALSE TRUE) 750
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 a multiple of a week` 2) (`test pay period facts` 0 29 FALSE TRUE) 750)
-- "the person has cash earnings for each week in the pay period": enough in total is not enough without it
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 a multiple of a week` 2) (`test pay period facts` 400 0 FALSE FALSE) 750)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 a multiple of a week` 2) (`test pay period facts` 0 30 FALSE FALSE) 750)
-- (b) semi-monthly: 2 1/6 times the amount (325) or 33 hours
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 a semi-monthly pay period` (`test pay period facts` 325 0 TRUE FALSE) 750
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 a semi-monthly pay period` (`test pay period facts` 324 0 TRUE FALSE) 750)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 a semi-monthly pay period` (`test pay period facts` 0 33 FALSE TRUE) 750
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 a semi-monthly pay period` (`test pay period facts` 0 32 FALSE TRUE) 750)
-- (c) monthly: 4 1/3 times the amount (650) or 65 hours
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 a monthly pay period` (`test pay period facts` 650 0 TRUE FALSE) 750
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 a monthly pay period` (`test pay period facts` 649 0 TRUE FALSE) 750)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 a monthly pay period` (`test pay period facts` 0 65 FALSE TRUE) 750
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 a monthly pay period` (`test pay period facts` 0 64 FALSE TRUE) 750)
-- (d) seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday: 20 per cent of the maximum (150), or 15 hours; no "each" needed
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` (`test pay period facts` 150 0 FALSE FALSE) 750
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` (`test pay period facts` 0 15 FALSE FALSE) 750
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` `er6 seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` (`test pay period facts` 149 14 TRUE TRUE) 750)
-- (e) more than one period of seven consecutive days (three here): the amount times 3 (450), or 15 times 3 (45) hours, for each period
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` 3) (`test pay period facts` 450 0 TRUE FALSE) 750
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` 3) (`test pay period facts` 449 0 TRUE FALSE) 750)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` 3) (`test pay period facts` 0 45 FALSE TRUE) 750
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` 3) (`test pay period facts` 0 44 FALSE TRUE) 750)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I s 6.1(2) the cash earnings or the hours reach what is required for the pay period` (`er6 more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` 3) (`test pay period facts` 450 45 FALSE FALSE) 750)

§ `Part I.1 -- s 12: prescribed weeks`

`test week facts` a1 a2 a3 a4 b1 b2 b3 b4 b5 c MEANS `er6 Facts about a week` WITH
    `workers’ compensation payments received or to be received, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim` IS a1
    `earnings under a wage-loss indemnity plan by reason of illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy or care of a child received or to be received` IS a2
    `indemnity payments referred to in paragraph 35(2)(f) received or to be received` IS a3
    `earnings because of which, under section 19 of the Act, no benefits are payable received or to be received` IS a4
    `attending a course or program of instruction or training to which the claimant was referred by the Commission or a designated authority` IS b1
    `employed under the Self-employment or Job Creation Partnerships employment benefit or a similar benefit under an agreement under section 63` IS b2
    `prevented from establishing an interruption of earnings by the allocation of earnings under section 36` IS b3
    `serving a week of the waiting period` IS b4
    `disqualified` IS b5
    `a week of unemployment due to a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the premises at which the claimant was employed` IS c

-- each of the ten ways, alone: (a)(i) to (iv), (b)(i) to (v), (c)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 10 6) (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- "applies ... during the period beginning on September 12, 1996 and ending on December 31, 1996"
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 9 11) (`test week facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 9 12) (`test week facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1996 12 31) (`test week facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(1) the week is a prescribed week for the purposes of paragraph 7(4)(c) of the Act` (YMD 1997 1 1) (`test week facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- (2): a week is taken into account once. Three weeks: one meets (a)(i) and (b)(v), one meets none, one meets (c): two prescribed weeks, not three
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(2) the number of prescribed weeks, each week taken into account once` (YMD 1996 10 6) (LIST (`test week facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE), (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE), (`test week facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part I.1 s 12(2) the number of prescribed weeks, each week taken into account once` (YMD 1996 10 6) (EMPTY) EQUALS 0

§ `Part II item 2 -- s 19: the record of employment`

#ASSERT `Regs Sch III Part II s 19(1) the employer must complete a record of employment` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part II s 19(1) the employer must complete a record of employment` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Regs Sch III Part II s 19(1) the employer must complete a record of employment` (YMD 1996 8 1) FALSE TRUE)
